kind honors, for marketplaces,\nindexes, "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"and crawlers. Repositories and packages carry the\n`dsh-plugin` GitHub topic and the same\ncanonical k"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"eywords (`deepseek-harness`, `dsh`, `dsh-plugin`, `cordis`)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Repository layout"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"`@yadsh` (Yet Another DSH) is a pnpm + Nx monorepo for independently versioned\nDeepSeek Harness plug"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ins. Each directory under `plugins/` is its own public npm\npackage; shared runtime libraries and wor"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"kspace tooling live under `packages/`."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Packages"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The table is generated from the workspace manifests. Published packages show\ntheir npm name and thei"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"r catalog kind — `DSH plugin` for a package\n`dsh plugin add` registers on a profile, `runtime librar"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"y` for a package a\nconsumer imports as a dependency. Private build tooling is not published, so it\ns"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"tays listed as a private workspace package with no kind."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Directory | npm package | Kind | Purpose |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| `plugins/dsh-answer-review-gate` | `@yadsh/dsh-answer-review-gate` | DSH plugin | Independent answ"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"er review gate for DeepSeek Harness agent responses |\n| `plugins/dsh-cas-results` | `@yadsh/dsh-cas-"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"results` | DSH plugin | Content-addressed offload store for bulky DeepSeek Harness tool results |\n| "},{"id":"p13s4","text":"`plugins/dsh-decision-tools` | `@yadsh/dsh-decision-tools` | DSH plugin | DeepSeek Harness decision,"},{"id":"p13s5","text":" classification, scoring and ranking tools for System One backends |\n| `plugins/dsh-doc-impact` | `@"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"yadsh/dsh-doc-impact` | DSH plugin | Deterministic documentation impact engine for DeepSeek Harness "},{"id":"p13s7","text":"|\n| `plugins/dsh-documents` | `@yadsh/dsh-documents` | DSH plugin | Managed document pipeline for th"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"e DeepSeek Harness: DOCX/PDF, XLSX/CSV/TSV/OpenDocument spreadsheets, Markdown and online sources as"},{"id":"p13s9","text":" agent tools |\n| `plugins/dsh-domain-experts` | `@yadsh/dsh-domain-experts` | DSH plugin | Configura"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"ble domain-scoped expert agents for DeepSeek Harness |\n| `plugins/dsh-draft-sessions` | `@yadsh/dsh-"},{"id":"p13s11","text":"draft-sessions` | DSH plugin | Persistent unsent draft sessions for DeepSeek Harness |\n| `plugins/ds"},{"id":"p13s12","text":"h-git-readonly` | `@yadsh/dsh-git-readonly` | DSH plugin | Read-only git provenance tools for DeepSe"},{"id":"p13s13","text":"ek Harness agents |\n| `plugins/dsh-humanizer` | `@yadsh/dsh-humanizer` | DSH plugin | Humanizer text"},{"id":"p13s14","text":" rewriting tools for DeepSeek Harness agents |\n| `plugins/dsh-jev-compaction` | `@yadsh/dsh-jev-comp"},{"id":"p13s15","text":"action` | DSH plugin | Jev/System-One semantic pruning of stale tool results for DeepSeek Harness; k"},{"id":"p13s16","text":"eeps conversation text verbatim and forgets stale tool output before summary compaction is needed |\n"},{"id":"p13s17","text":"| `plugins/dsh-kv-persist` | `@yadsh/dsh-kv-persist` | DSH plugin | Persistent KV-cache/session-stat"},{"id":"p13s18","text":"e manager for DeepSeek Harness (llama.cpp slot snapshots) |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Requirements: Node.js 22 or newer and pnpm 10.4.1."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Nx runs project-local `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`, and `verify` scripts and caches\ntheir ou"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"tputs. The dependency check enforces workspace boundaries, while the\ntarball check packs every publi"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"c package, validates its manifest and exported\nfiles, and installs it in a clean consumer project."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"`plugins.json` and the package table above are generated from the workspace\nmanifests. Regenerate bo"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"th after changing a package description, keywords, or\nthe package set — `pnpm verify:packages` fails"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" while either catalog is stale:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Adding a plugin"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The generator defaults to the `@yadsh` npm scope and creates the package,\nCordis patch, build config"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"uration, tests, and public-package metadata. The\nscaffold is a starting point: before writing code, "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"read the\nplugin guidelines — the canonical architecture,\npackage-content, testing, documentation, an"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"d release rules every plugin must\nfollow. Run `pnpm plugins:manifest` afterwards so the new package "},{"id":"p22s5","text":"ry plugin must\nfollow. Run `pnpm plugins:manifest` afterwards so the new package enters the\ncatalog."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- Architecture overview — layout, host/client split, build outputs, dependency rules\n- Plugin guidel"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ines — the canonical rulebook every plugin must follow\n- Plugin logging — file logging API, formats,"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" levels, console mirror\n- Verification runbook — what each gate asserts, locally and in CI\n- Test co"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"verage — what `pnpm test:coverage` measures, and the last committed snapshot per package\n- Releasing"},{"id":"p24s5","text":" and compatibility policy"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Releases"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Packages use independent Nx Version Plans:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The GitHub release workflow builds and verifies selected package tarballs before\npublishing through "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"npm Trusted Publishing. See the release runbook\nand compatibility policy."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"